s390/vfio_ccw: Ensure index for read/write regions are within range

jira KERNEL-1718
Rebuild_History Non-Buildable kernel-4.18.0-553.171.1.el8_10
commit-author Eric Farman <farman@linux.ibm.com>
commit 9f5f9a78fedc45bc29d6a0a64e3a3472361afae5
Empty-Commit: Cherry-Pick Conflicts during history rebuild.
Will be included in final tarball splat. Ref for failed cherry-pick at:
ciq/ciq_backports/kernel-4.18.0-553.171.1.el8_10/9f5f9a78.failed

The introduction of the capability chain rightly clamped the
region indexes to the range of the capabilities itself, but
neglected to do so for the existing read/write regions which
should also be enforced.

Fixes: db8e5d17ac03 ("vfio-ccw: add capabilities chain")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
	Cc: Cornelia Huck <cohuck@redhat.com>
	Reviewed-by: Matthew Rosato <mjrosato@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Eric Farman <farman@linux.ibm.com>
	Signed-off-by: Christian Borntraeger <borntraeger@linux.ibm.com>
(cherry picked from commit 9f5f9a78fedc45bc29d6a0a64e3a3472361afae5)
	Signed-off-by: Jonathan Maple <jmaple@ciq.com>

# Conflicts:
#	drivers/s390/cio/vfio_ccw_async.c
#	drivers/s390/cio/vfio_ccw_chp.c
diff --cc drivers/s390/cio/vfio_ccw_async.c
